# B4s — A VILLAGE: EVERY STRUCTURE IN THE WINDOW, BY PEELING
#
# ⛔ **`B4o` ASKED FOR THIS PICTURE AND SAID THE CORPUS DID NOT HAVE IT** — *"a window
# with three structures describes the house and one of the other two. What decides
# whether that matters is a picture of a village."*
#
# ⚠ **`B4p` MEASURED THE COST EXACTLY.** A closed rim contributes no chain ENDS, so
# `wall_read_run` sees only the wall's two and answers for the wall — correctly, with the
# tower's 54 marks unmentioned. The peel takes each description's own marks out before
# asking the next question, so the rim is alone by the time it is asked about.
#
# ⚠ **AND THE ORDER IN THE CAPTION IS THE CHAIN'S, NOT THE SCENE'S**: house, then run,
# then disc. The house is first because the round readers refuse a field holding one.
#
#   make plan-view WORLD=b4s Q0=-12 Q1=13 R0=-16 R1=10 REF=2.0

echo --- a house
at 0 0 90
verb place

echo --- a round tower, six clear cells south of it
at 0 -12 0
verb tower

echo --- and a wall down the west side
at -9 -3 0
verb run
at -9 6 0
verb run
